# 1. Vision

MAYA is a software trust analysis platform built from SBOM data.

Its purpose is to transform software inventory information into an explainable, auditable and reproducible assessment of:

- technical risk;
- software governance;
- software supply-chain risk;
- geopolitical exposure;
- critical dependencies;
- overall software trust.

The target architecture is:

SBOM
↓
Canonical Model
↓
Enrichment
↓
Package Identity Resolution
↓
Project Resolution
↓
Governance Resolution
↓
Geographic Facts
↓
Trust Events
↓
Trust Assessment
↓
COMEX / Excel Reporting

The final geopolitical analysis is European-centric, with particular attention to dependencies on organizations, infrastructure and jurisdictions outside Europe.

No geopolitical conclusion may be inferred solely from a namespace, name, domain name, repository host or programming language.

